    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d952">

                <pb facs="0814" n="806" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg806"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.9431/140: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-17T16:00:00+09:00">December 17, 1937—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 17—9:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>649. Department’s 351, December 16, 3 p.m.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d952-f1"/></p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>We have, on several occasions when discussing at the Foreign Office
                        Japanese exchange control and regulation of imports and exports, <pb
                            facs="0815" n="807" xml:id="pg807"/> pointed out that these measures are
                        not in harmony with American efforts to liberalize trade. We expressed doubt
                        whether there would be any basis for a trade agreement with the United
                        States so long as any tariff concession which Japan might make could be made
                        valueless by exchange and import control.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Yoshizawa,<anchor n="17" xml:id="d952-f2"/> with whom these discussions
                        were held, fully understands the position and in fact indicated that the
                        Japanese Government is not giving active consideration to proposing a trade
                        agreement with the United States. Nevertheless we will take an early
                        opportunity to clarify the situation.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
